Training 1 – Stratified Sampling (checkpoints_v5)
Version 4 ki first training mein humne MILK10k dataset ki 11 classes aur dono modalities, dermoscopic aur clinical close-up images, use ki thi. 
Dataset mein total 5,240 lesions the, jinhein stratified splitting ke through 70% training (3,668), 15% validation (786) aur 15% testing (786) mein 
divide kiya gaya tha, taake har subset mein classes ka proportion maintain rahe. Model mein dual-branch Spiking VGG-13 architecture, Global Average 
Pooling aur non-spiking classification head use hua. Training ke liye Adam optimizer, learning rate 0.0001 aur cross-entropy loss use ki gayi. 
Is training mein batch size 4 tha aur total 10 epochs successfully complete hue. Final epoch mein 57.88% training accuracy aur 1.3059 training loss achieve hua, 
jabke validation accuracy 48.35% aur validation loss 1.5186 record hua. Lekin classification report analyze karne par pata chala ke model predominantly 
BCC class predict kar raha tha, jiska recall 100% tha, jabke almost saari remaining classes ka recall zero tha. Isse ye clear hua ke stratified splitting 
ke bawajood class imbalance ka issue resolve nahi hua tha. Stratified splitting ne dataset ke different subsets mein class proportions preserve kiye, 
lekin minority classes ko training ke dauran equal representation nahi di. Consequently, model majority class ki taraf biased raha aur different skin 
diseases ke distinguishing features effectively learn nahi kar saka.
Training 2 – Weighted Random Sampler (checkpoints_v6)
First training mein class imbalance aur majority-class prediction bias observe karne ke baad second training mein humne Weighted Random Sampler 
introduce kiya, taake minority classes ko training ke dauran select hone ka zyada chance mil sake. Is approach mein class frequencies ke inverse proportion 
mein sampling weights assign kiye gaye, jisse minority classes ki representation increase ho aur model sirf majority class par depend na kare. 
Is training mein batch size 1 tha, jiski wajah se ek epoch mein total 3,668 batches the. Training procedure mein epoch-wise validation aur best-model 
checkpoint saving bhi include ki gayi. Lekin second training ke saved outputs mein learning performance mein koi significant improvement observe nahi hui. 
First epoch ke initial batches mein average loss approximately 2.4361 tha, jo gradually decrease hokar batch 3,650/3,668 par 2.3879 tak pohancha. 
Yani 3,650 batches process hone ke bawajood loss mein sirf approximately 0.0482 ki reduction hui aur woh abhi bhi relatively high tha. Isse indicate 
hota hai ke Weighted Random Sampler introduce karne ke baad bhi model ki learning satisfactory nahi thi. Halanke loss mein slight decrease nazar aaya, 
lekin isse meaningful classification improvement confirm nahi hoti. Notebook mein second training ki completed epoch accuracy aur validation results available 
nahi hain, isliye ye conclude nahi kiya ja sakta ke minority-class predictions improve hui ya nahi. Available batch outputs se sirf itna establish hota hai 
ke Weighted Random Sampler use karne ke bawajood initial training progress limited thi aur model ki effective learning abhi bhi concern thi.
